## How Cluster Points Work

KUCCPS uses **weighted cluster points (WCP)** — not your raw KCSE aggregate — to rank applicants per programme.

- Each programme specifies **4 cluster subjects**
- Your grades in those 4 subjects are weighted against the top candidates nationally
- Points are computed to **3 decimal places** to minimise ties
- The **cut-off point** = WCP of the last student competitively placed in a course at a given university

### Grading Scale (for manual estimation only)
| Grade | Points |
|-------|--------|
| A | 12 |
| A- | 11 |
| B+ | 10 |
| B | 9 |
| B- | 8 |
| C+ | 7 |
| C | 6 |
| C- | 5 |
| D+ | 4 |
| D | 3 |
| D- | 2 |
| E | 1 |

> **Important:** Do not calculate your own WCP manually. Log in at [students.kuccps.net](https://students.kuccps.net) — KUCCPS calculates it automatically and shows it per programme.

**Minimum mean grade for degree programmes: C+**

