## Quick Tips for Applicants

1. **Always check the portal.** Log in at [students.kuccps.net](https://students.kuccps.net) to see your actual WCP per programme alongside 2022, 2023, and 2024 cutoffs for comparison.

2. **Use the 3-university structure for your first choice.** Pick the same course at 3 different universities (e.g., 1a = UoN, 1b = KU, 1c = JKUAT) to maximise your chances of getting the course you want.

3. **Apply for up to 6 programme choices.** Mix courses and universities across your 2nd, 3rd, and 4th choices as backup options.

4. **A WCP of 0.000 means you didn't take a mandatory cluster subject.** Only apply to programmes where you have all four required cluster subjects.

5. **Government sponsorship priority** goes to candidates who sat KCSE in the preceding year and have not previously benefited.

6. **Cutoffs change every year.** A high cutoff this year can drop next year depending on applications, slot availability, and national performance — don't rule out a course based on last year's data alone.

7. **Lesser-known universities have lower cutoffs for the same programme.** If your points are borderline, consider institutions outside Nairobi for the same degree — you can always transfer or specialise later.

